<title>UK: London sugar freight market has holiday slowdown.</title>
<headline>London sugar freight market has holiday slowdown.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The sugar freight market quietened considerably as the Easter holiday period closed in with fresh fixtures difficult to find and new orders rather thin, brokers said.</p>
<p>The new orders included Dreyfus looking for tonnage from Guatemala to Yemen for mid-April and another 25,000 bulk Cuba to Black Sea or Baltic mid-April.</p>
<p>Cargill were looking to cover 14,000 bagged N.Brazil to Lagos for early April and E D and F Man 3,000/6,000 bagged E.Coast Mexico to Angola for first half April.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
